\title{pord: Exact Conditional Tests for Paired Ordinal Data on a Square Table}
\description{
Exact conditional tests for paired ordinal data recorded on the same K-point scale, such as expectation and achievement rated by the same respondent. The primary test asks whether the number of pairs with y >= x exceeds what independence would give, conditioning on both margins of the K x K table. This is a generalization of Fisher's exact test: it uses the same conditioning (the Fisher-Yates multiple hypergeometric distribution) and reduces to Fisher's exact test when the scale is dichotomized, but the test statistic counts one direction only. The null distribution is obtained exactly by dynamic programming, with permutation and closed-form normal approximations available as alternatives; the null mean and variance have closed forms depending only on the two margins. Companion functions provide the sign test for y < x (with a conditional variant that removes the ceiling bias), group comparison by label permutation, and diagnostics for how the margins govern power.
}
